.TH "REMOTEPLAYBACK.CONNECT_EVENT" "3JS" "October 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
RemotePlayback.connect_event \- RemotePlayback: connect event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]connect\f[B]\f[R] event of the \f[CR]RemotePlayback\f[R]
interface fires when the user agent connects to the remote device.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqconnect\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
onconnect = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A generic \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLE
In the following example the value of \f[CR]RemotePlayback.state\f[R] is
printed to the console when the user agent successfully connects.
.IP
.EX
RemotePlayback.onconnect = () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(RemotePlayback.state);
};
.EE
